{"schemaVersion":1,"sourceRecord":{"schemaVersion":1,"recordId":"wikibooks-23675-r4615138","sourceId":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa","sourceTitle":"Cookbook:Mango Atchar","sourcePageId":23675,"sourceRevision":"4615138","sourceRevisionTimestamp":"2026-02-03T02:23:41Z","sourceRevisionUser":"Kittycataclysm","sourceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/w/index.php?title=Cookbook:Mango%20Atchar&oldid=4615138","retrievedAt":"2026-10-13T13:08:24.620Z","sourceCategories":["Category:Recipes","Category:Recipes for curry","Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments","Category:Recipes using coriander","Category:Recipes using curry leaf","Category:Recipes using curry powder","Category:Recipes using fructose","Category:Recipes using ground cumin","Category:Recipes using honey","Category:Recipes using mango","Category:Recipes using mustard seed","Category:Recipes using sunflower oil","Category:Recipes with metric units","Category:Recipes without cooking time","Category:Recipes without servings","Category:South African recipes","Category:Very Easy recipes"],"license":{"id":"wikibooks-cookbook-cc-by-sa-4.0","name":"Creative Commons Attribution-ShareAlike 4.0 International (CC BY-SA 4.0); Wikibooks text is generally dual-licensed with GFDL unless otherwise noted","evidenceUrl":"https://en.wikibooks.org/wiki/Wikibooks:Copyrights","policyStatus":"verified-license","pageExceptionStatus":"not-reviewed-per-page","attribution":"Attribute Wikibooks contributors by linking each version-specific source page. Indicate that structured fields are extracted and any translated or edited text is modified. Include CC BY-SA 4.0 notice/link and share adaptations under CC BY-SA 4.0 or later.","changeNoticeRequired":true,"shareAlikeRequired":true},"sourceSha256":"2da41274c8c034379e37253bbf876b030f3bcb42f6a4061b080ff028849e17a3","sourceWikitext":"{{Recipe summary\n| Category = Condiment recipes\n| Difficulty = 1\n}}\n\n{{recipe}} | [[Cookbook:Cuisine of South Africa|South Africa]] | [[Cookbook:Sausage|Sausage]]\n\n'''Atchar''' is a spicy condiment, often eaten with a curry. It comes from the Indian cuisine in South Africa. In India, it is spelled Achar, and the word means pickle in Hindi. Usually the atchar made in South Africa is made with unripe green mangoes and chillies. The whole mango is used for making atchar.\n\nThis traditional mango atchar is easily made at home. Adjust the amount of chillies to your liking and serve with a vegetable curry, or on a slice of white bread.\n\n== Ingredients ==\n\n* 1.5 [[Cookbook:Kilogram|kg]] unripe [[Cookbook:Mango|mangoes]], [[Cookbook:Chopping|chopped]]\n* 4 [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] garlic and herb salt\n* 3 [[Cookbook:Tablespoon|Tbsp]] [[Cookbook:Chili Powder|chilli powder]]\n* 2 Tbsp [[Cookbook:Cumin|cumin]] powder\n* 1 Tbsp ground [[Cookbook:Coriander|coriander]]\n* 3 Tbsp [[Cookbook:Curry Powder|curry powder]]\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cups]] (360 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) raw [[Cookbook:Honey|honey]] or [[Cookbook:Fructose|fructose]]\n* 2 cups (480 ml) [[Cookbook:Balsamic vinegar|balsamic vinegar]]\n* ½ cup (120 [[Cookbook:Gram|g]]) [[Cookbook:Cornstarch|corn]] or [[Cookbook:Potato Starch|potato starch]]\n* 2 Tbsp [[Cookbook:Mustard seed|mustard seeds]]\n* 1 handful [[Cookbook:Curry Leaf|curry leaves]]\n* 1½ cups (360 [[Cookbook:Milliliter|ml]]) virgin [[Cookbook:Olive Oil|olive oil]] or cold-pressed [[Cookbook:Sunflower Oil|sunflower oil]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# [[Cookbook:Simmering|Simmer]] all the ingredients except the mangoes and the oil until thickened.\n# Pour mixture over the mangoes, add the oil, and mix well.\n# Cool and refrigerate for at least 12 hours.\n\n[[Category:Recipes for curry|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes for sauces and condiments|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mango|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:South African recipes|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes_with_metric_units|{{PAGENAME}}]]\n[[Category:Recipes using coriander]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry leaf]]\n[[Category:Recipes using curry powder]]\n[[Category:Recipes using fructose]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cumin]]\n[[Category:Recipes using sunflower oil]]\n[[Category:Recipes using honey]]\n[[Category:Recipes using mustard seed]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Mango Atchar","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"1.5 kg unripe mangoes, chopped","sourceText":"1.5 kg unripe mangoes, chopped","amountText":"1.5 kg unripe mangoes, chopped","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-2","name":"4 tsp garlic and herb salt","sourceText":"4 tsp garlic and herb salt","amountText":"4 tsp garlic and herb salt","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-3","name":"3 Tbsp chilli powder","sourceText":"3 Tbsp chilli powder","amountText":"3 Tbsp chilli powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-4","name":"2 Tbsp cumin powder","sourceText":"2 Tbsp cumin powder","amountText":"2 Tbsp cumin powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-5","name":"1 Tbsp ground coriander","sourceText":"1 Tbsp ground coriander","amountText":"1 Tbsp ground coriander","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-6","name":"3 Tbsp curry powder","sourceText":"3 Tbsp curry powder","amountText":"3 Tbsp curry powder","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-7","name":"1½ cups (360 ml) raw honey or fructose","sourceText":"1½ cups (360 ml) raw honey or fructose","amountText":"1½ cups (360 ml) raw honey or fructose","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-8","name":"2 cups (480 ml) balsamic vinegar","sourceText":"2 cups (480 ml) balsamic vinegar","amountText":"2 cups (480 ml) balsamic vinegar","amount":null,"unit":null,"foodBinding":null},{"id":"source-line-9","name":"½ cup (120 g) corn or potato starch","sourceText":"½ cup (120 g) corn or potato starch","amountText":"½ cup (120 g) corn or potato starch","amount"